                <pb facs="0781" n="769" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg769"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.79682/3: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Liberia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Wharton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-10-18T18:00:00-05:00">October 18, 1940—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>42. Your 55, September 19, 9 a.m. Department has informed the President of Pan
                    American Airways and the President of American Export Airlines of the desire of
                    the Liberian Government to discuss the practicability of undertaking air
                    transport services between the United States and Liberia.</p>
                <p>In making this statement for the information of these companies, the Department
                    has pointed out that it cannot undertake to indicate what the attitude of the
                    Civil Aeronautics Board would be in the event that either company should apply
                    to the Board for a certificate authorizing an air transport service to
                    Liberia.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
